---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import RichTextEditorDemo from '../../components/RichTextEditorDemo';
---

<Docs
  title="Rich Text Editor"
  description="A chat message editor built on Tiptap: Enter sends, Markdown-style shortcuts format, and a toolbar slot holds pickers and the send button."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Rich Text Editor</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The message box behind the chat composer. Enter sends, Shift+Enter adds a line, and headings, lists, links, and code
    fences work as you type. Put it in a composer <code>InputGroup</code> and hand it a toolbar.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <RichTextEditorDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Rich Text Editor usage"
      code={`import {
  RichTextEditor,
  type RichTextEditorHandle,
  type RichTextValue,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/rich-text-editor";

// A local draft with a formatting toolbar
const editor = useRef<RichTextEditorHandle>(null);
const [value, setValue] = useState<RichTextValue>({ type: "doc", content: [{ type: "paragraph" }] });

<RichTextEditor ref={editor} value={value} onChange={setValue} onSend={send}
  placeholder="Write a local draft…"
  toolbarAddon={<>
    <Button variant="ghost" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Bold"
      aria-pressed={editor.current?.editor()?.isActive("bold") ?? false}
      onClick={() => editor.current?.editor()?.chain().focus().toggleMark("bold").run()}>
      <Bold aria-hidden="true" />
    </Button>
    <Button variant="outline" size="sm" onClick={send}>Send <Send aria-hidden="true" /></Button>
  </>} />

// Compact, without a toolbar
<RichTextEditor size="compact" value={value} onChange={setValue} onSend={send} />

// Inside the chat composer
<InputGroup variant={questionPending ? "question-composer" : "composer"}>
  {attachments && <InputGroupAddon align="block-start">{attachments}</InputGroupAddon>}
  <RichTextEditor
    key={compact ? "compact" : "full"}
    ref={inputRef}
    size={compact ? "compact" : "default"}
    condensed={questionPending && !focused && !attachments && !canSend}
    placeholder={questionPending ? "Send a separate message…" : "Ask anything…"}
    value={value}
    onChange={setValue}
    onSend={send}
    disabled={disabled || sending}
    ariaInvalid={!!validation}
    ariaDescribedBy={validation ? errorId : undefined}
    ariaExpanded={!!suggestions}
    ariaControls={suggestions?.id}
    ariaActiveDescendant={suggestions?.activeId}
    extensions={compact ? mentionNodes : [...mentionNodes, fileSuggestion, skillSuggestion]}
    toolbarAddon={<>
      <FileChoices />
      <ModelPicker />
      <InputGroupButton type="submit" size="icon-sm"
        variant={canSend ? "default" : "secondary"} aria-label="Send message">
        <ArrowUp aria-hidden="true" />
      </InputGroupButton>
    </>}
  />
</InputGroup>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>value</code> is a Tiptap JSON document and <code>onChange</code>
      gets the new one on every edit. A new <code>value</code> from outside replaces the content without calling{' '}
      <code>onChange</code>.<code>onSend</code> runs on Enter and on Cmd or Ctrl+Enter.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>size</code> is <code>default</code> (80px to 256px, 16px text, a toolbar row below) or <code>compact</code>{' '}
      (40px to 128px, 14px text, the toolbar inline at the end). <code>condensed</code> shrinks a default editor to the
      same single row, such as while an agent question waits. Past the maximum height the editor scrolls.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>toolbarAddon</code> holds buttons and pickers.
      <code>extensions</code> adds Tiptap extensions, such as mention nodes and
      <code>@</code> or <code>/</code> suggestion triggers. Pass a stable array with
      <code>useMemo</code>; a new array rebuilds the editor.
      <code>placeholder</code> defaults to <code>Ask anything…</code> and can change while mounted.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> stops editing and dims the editor.
      <code>ariaLabel</code> (default <code>Message</code>),
      <code>ariaInvalid</code>, <code>ariaDescribedBy</code>,<code>ariaControls</code>, and{' '}
      <code>ariaActiveDescendant</code> go on the textbox.
      <code>ariaExpanded</code> tells the editor a suggestion list is open; it isn't written to the DOM, because ARIA
      doesn't allow
      <code>aria-expanded</code> on a textbox.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <code>ref</code> handle has <code>focus()</code>,<code>editor()</code> for Tiptap commands, and
      <code>setContent(doc)</code>, which replaces the document and calls
      <code>onChange</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Behavior</h2>
    <p>
      Enter sends unless the caret is in a list item or code block, a suggestion list is open (<code>ariaExpanded</code>
      ), or the line is a bare code fence. Shift+Enter adds a line break; Cmd or Ctrl+Enter always sends. Enter during
      IME composition never sends.
    </p>
    <p>
      Headings go up to level 3. Typing <code>```sql</code> and Space starts a code block, even after a Shift+Enter line
      break. Pasted text with
      <code>```</code> or <code>~~~</code> fences becomes code blocks. Links allow only <code>http</code>,{' '}
      <code>https</code>, and
      <code>mailto</code>, don't open on click, and stop extending once you type past them. There is no underline or
      horizontal rule.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The editor is a multi-line <code>textbox</code> with
      <code>aria-autocomplete="list"</code>. Point
      <code>ariaControls</code> at a suggestion listbox and
      <code>ariaActiveDescendant</code> at its active option, so screen readers follow arrow keys while focus stays in
      the text. Name icon-only toolbar buttons with
      <code>aria-label</code> and show pressed formats with <code>aria-pressed</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      On its own the editor shows a 2px focus outline. Inside an
      <code>InputGroup</code> it is marked
      <code>data-slot="input-group-control"</code>, so the group draws focus and invalid borders instead. Fades take
      120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. Forced colors mode keeps a system focus outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Text uses <code>--sprout-text</code>, the placeholder and quotes
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, code backgrounds
      <code>--sprout-hover</code>, and links <code>--sprout-primary</code>. The toolbar divider is{' '}
      <code>--sprout-line</code> and focus
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>. The opt-in TulipFarm theme tints links and the send button through these tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
